            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "Why do nitrogen oxides form in a petrol engine even though petrol contains no nitrogen?",
            "explanation": "The air drawn into the engine is four-fifths nitrogen; at the high temperature of combustion some of it reacts with oxygen, N2 + O2 giving 2NO, which is then oxidised to NO2 in the exhaust and the air."
